From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 04f0: gpu_timing: cheap per-phase GPU timestamps at the guest render markers, exported frame time, draw experiments, in-run cvar cycle

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (stream LOCK60 A1/A2). Validated in game: runs lk-cm1 (cost model), lk-vrs1, lk-gov1/2, lk-val1
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: D3D12. Cvars (GPU/Timing): gpu_timing (0; 1 = timestamps at every guest render marker / phase cut, per-segment counters,
  '[gpu-timing]' log every gpu_timing_log_s, optional per-frame CSV gpu_timing_csv), gpu_timing_export (true: with gpu_timing 0 only
  the frame's start/end + list-boundary timestamps, one tiny resolve, no counters), gpu_draw_experiment (0; 1 zero-area scissor,
  2 guest draw not recorded, 3 first primitive + zero scissor) with gpu_draw_experiment_phases (phase mask), gpu_experiment_cycle /
  _period_ms / _start_s / _repeat (an in-run schedule of cvar assignments, switched at frame boundaries, frame-exact tagging).
  Data exports of rexgpu-xenos.dll: rexgpu_gpu_frame_us, rexgpu_gpu_frame_seq, rexgpu_gpu_frame_lag (the game's governor reads
  them) and rexgpu_vrs_level / rexgpu_vrs_levels (used by 0500). Experiments and full timing off by default = no change but the
  export's timestamps.
Bucket: REDO

04f0-gpu-timing.patch (mcla-x86 LOCK60). 0510 changes the exported value to the GPU busy time (see there).

---
